{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed automobile garage (Use Class B2), due to its inappropriate location outside a designated employment area and its adverse impact on existing uses, notably the Public House at No.51, resulting from the sub-division of the site would be an unacceptable form of development and which fails to comply with Local Plan Policies ED1 and CI1",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposal, due to its poor design, scale, and nature of use, has lead to a bulky, cramped and obtrusive form of development that harms the character and appearance of the site, public streetscene and surrounding area. It would be contrary to Local Plan policies CC1 and CC2",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed development has failed to demonstrate, by virtue of its inappropriate location, use and absence of technical justification, that it would have an acceptable impact upon neighbours living conditions in terms of noise and pollution, the proposal would run contrary to Local Plan policies CC1, CC2, EQ3 and EQ5",
    "Reason : 4 - The proposal has not sufficiently demonstrated that adequate arrangements would be provided with regards to parking, delivery and servicing, and refuse and recycling management for the various uses on site in a manner that would not prejudice the safe and efficient operation of the premises and local road networks. This would be contrary to London Plan Policies T5, T6 and T7; and Local Plan Policies EC2 and EQ7"
  ],
